    "text": "A local app does not need a backend. A server becomes useful when records are shared under authentication, when a private service credential is needed, or when an operation must be controlled outside the editable client.\n\nThe repository has two server hosts that run server-side `.logic` with SQLite: the Rust private backend (`apps/softn-host-rust`) and the PHP host (`apps/softn-host-php`), which the single-app backend archives package. Server logic is JavaScript on both; Python is client logic only. FormLogic is a separate connected host with its own configuration."
